        "# Pipeline Parallel and Bubble Analysis Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `PipelineStage`: a small `nn.Module` that holds one stage's parameters and exposes `forward(activation)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Pipeline(stages, num_microbatches)`: orchestrates the GPipe schedule on simulated stages using simulated wall-clock per stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `bubble_fraction(num_stages, num_microbatches)`: closed-form (N-1)/(M+N-1)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A 4-stage demo that prints the per-microbatch trace and the measured bubble fraction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: a stage-by-microbatch Gantt chart and the bubble percentage against the closed-form prediction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Implement 1F1B and verify the bubble fraction matches GPipe but activation memory is bounded.\n2. Profile real per-stage time on a deeper model and rebalance stages by measured wall-clock.\n3. Add gradient accumulation across pipeline microbatches and check the gradient equals the gradient of the equivalent full-batch forward.\n4. Pair the pipeline with activation checkpointing and measure the memory drop versus compute cost.\n5. Combine pipeline with DDP (each pipeline rank is replicated across a data-parallel group) and reason through the 2D schedule."
      ]
    }
